  "limits": {
    "rounds": 12,
    "rounds_max": 12,
    "actions_max": 1000,
    "deadline_s": 120
  },
  "rules": "VISIBILITY. Your private hand, your colour totals (red, blue, green) and your gold are known only to you. The order of the deck is known to nobody. Public: the deck composition, every lot, every talk message and who wrote it, every bid, every auction result and price, every player's bought list, every Church choice and who made it, and the colour VP values. Kept Gold cards are never revealed; all gold is revealed at scoring.\n\nSETUP. The deck holds {deck_size} cards: red, blue and green, each with values 1,1,2,2,3,4 (written like 'red-1'), {colour_cards} cards; Gold cards with values 2,2,3,3 (written like 'gold-2'), {gold_cards} cards; and {church_cards} Church cards ('church'). The deck is shuffled once at the start and never again. Each player starts with {starting_gold} gold, an empty private hand, an empty public bought list, red, blue and green totals of 0 and 0 vp. Red, blue and green each start worth {starting_colour_vp} VP.\n\nEACH ROUND ({rounds} rounds). In round r the active seat is ((r-1) mod 3)+1, so seats go 1,2,3,1,2,3,... and each seat is active exactly {turns_active_per_seat} times. The first {cards_drawn_per_round} cards of the deck are drawn; only the active player sees them.\n\nKEEP. The active player alone chooses one of the two drawn cards to keep. The kept card goes into their private hand and is never announced: a colour card adds its value to their matching colour total; a Gold card adds its value to their gold; a Church card means they make a Church choice this round. The other drawn card becomes the lot and is announced to everyone.\n\nTALK. All three players, including the active player, each write one short message at the same moment, without seeing the others' messages. All three messages are then shown to everyone with who wrote them. Nothing said is binding: propose prices, alliances or Church moves, bluff about your hand, or say nothing useful.\n\nAUCTION. The two non-active players at the same moment each secretly bid a whole number from 0 up to their own current gold. The active player does not bid. If one bid is strictly greater than the other and is at least {min_winning_bid}, that bidder wins the lot: they pay their bid from their gold to the active player's gold, the lot is added to their public bought list, and a colour lot adds its value to their matching total, a Gold lot adds its value to their gold, and a Church lot means they make a Church choice this round. If the two bids are equal (including both 0), nobody pays and the lot is discarded. Both bids and the result (the winner and the price, or 'discarded') are announced to everyone.\n\nCHURCH. Every player who gained a Church card this round (at most {church_choices_max_per_round}: the active player through a kept Church, the lot winner through a bought Church) chooses, at the same moment, one of: red up, red down, blue up, blue down, green up, green down. For each colour, the number of 'up' choices minus the number of 'down' choices this round is added to that colour's VP value, and the result is then kept between {vp_min} and {vp_max} (clamped once). All choices are announced with who made them. A player without a Church card this round is not asked.\n\nEND. After round {rounds} the deck is empty. All hands, colour totals and gold are revealed. For each colour, if one player's total is strictly higher than both others, that player adds that colour's current VP value to their vp. If the highest total is tied between two or more players, nobody scores that colour. The highest vp wins. A tie on vp is broken by more remaining gold. If that is also tied, the tied players share the win (a draw)."
}
